\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Overview of Adaptive Scout-Guided Dense Evidence (Adaptive SGDE).} Long untrimmed videos are first rapidly scanned by an ultra-lightweight 1.04B scout at 1.0~FPS. Video-adaptive $Z$-score normalization and hysteresis energy mining extract candidate action proposals, which are unified via sub-linear duration-adaptive windowing ($\Delta (T) \propto \ln T, G(T) \propto \sqrt  {T}$) and soft continuity merging. The focused candidate corridor is decoded with dense frames by a frozen 8B Vision-Language model with schema-delimited JSON syntax, eliminating background distractors while preserving cardinality.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline_intro}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
